{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat README.md package.json apps/desktop/package.json packages/desktop-contracts/package.json rust-toolchain.toml; cat apps/desktop/src/modules/academy/presentation-storage.ts; sed -n '500,700p' crates/desktop-core/src/store.rs; sed -n '1,140p' crates/desktop-core/src/store.rs; cat tools/p10/test_review_gate.py | tail -25\"","aggregated_output":"# Prisma AIRS Desktop v2\n\nSuccessor to Prisma AIRS Desktop: React presentation in Tauri, a focused Rust\napplication core, the native Rust SCM SDK, and shared Academy presentation.\nFirst target: macOS Apple Silicon, distributed as a signed and notarized DMG.\nImplementation proceeds through ordered, independently reviewed chunks; see\n[status](docs/planning/status.md) for what exists and what is verified.\n\nFor the current Worf VM transition, start with [WORF-START-HERE](docs/planning/WORF-START-HERE.md). It includes the exact source/worktree checkpoint verifier.\n\n## Layout\n\n```text\ncrates/desktop-core/          Rust application core: native authority, wire DTOs\napps/desktop/src-tauri/       desktop-host: Tauri window/origin admission, menus\napps/desktop/src/             React application composition\npackages/desktop-contracts/   generated wire declarations, typed facade, fixtures\ncrates/xtask/                 build-time check/review/completion controller\ntools/reference-validator/    one-off independent C01 bootstrap validator\n```\n\n## Building from a clean checkout\n\n```text\ncorepack enable pnpm --install-directory .tools/bin      # pnpm 10.6.5 (packageManager)\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- fetch-inputs --source <path to ai-security-academy clone>\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- check --chunk C01 --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- test  --chunk C01 --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\n```\n\nThe controller runs only the argv commands in\n[checks.json](docs/architecture/checks.json) under the environment contract in\n[toolchain.json](docs/architecture/toolchain.json); it never reads `.env` files.\n\nStart with the [implementation plan](docs/planning/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md),\n[chunk instructions](docs/planning/chunks/README.md), [decisions](docs/planning/decisions.md),\nthe [design](docs/architecture/DESIGN.md) and [ADRs](docs/adr/0001-native-operation-authority.md).\nNewly authored material uses [Apache-2.0](LICENSE); upstream terms remain intact.\nIndependent review: Codex reviews every chunk and phase (D026).\n\nOwner-specified repository:\n`ssh://git@git-ssh.cdot.io/cdot/prisma-airs-desktop-v2.git`.\n{\n  \"name\": \"prisma-airs-desktop\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"license\": \"Apache-2.0\",\n  \"packageManager\": \"pnpm@10.6.5\",\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \"24.21.0\"\n  },\n  \"pnpm\": {\n    \"peerDependencyRules\": {\n      \"allowedVersions\": {\n        \"react\": \"19.2.3\",\n        \"react-dom\": \"19.2.3\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\"\n}\n{\n  \"name\": \"@prisma-airs/desktop\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"license\": \"Apache-2.0\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json\",\n    \"build\": \"vite build\",\n    \"test\": \"vitest run --config vitest.config.ts\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@ai-security-academy/learner\": \"file:../../.work/academy/packages/learner\",\n    \"@ai-security-academy/presentation\": \"file:../../.work/academy/packages/presentation\",\n    \"@ai-security-academy/shared\": \"file:../../.work/academy/packages/shared\",\n    \"@codemirror/commands\": \"6.10.4\",\n    \"@codemirror/lang-python\": \"6.2.1\",\n    \"@codemirror/lang-yaml\": \"6.1.3\",\n    \"@codemirror/language\": \"6.12.4\",\n    \"@codemirror/state\": \"6.7.1\",\n    \"@codemirror/view\": \"6.43.5\",\n    \"@dnd-kit/core\": \"6.3.1\",\n    \"@excalidraw/excalidraw\": \"0.18.1\",\n    \"@fontsource-variable/caveat\": \"5.2.8\",\n    \"@fontsource-variable/inter\": \"5.2.8\",\n    \"@fontsource-variable/jetbrains-mono\": \"5.2.8\",\n    \"@lezer/highlight\": \"1.2.3\",\n    \"@prisma-airs/desktop-contracts\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@radix-ui/react-dialog\": \"1.1.20\",\n    \"@radix-ui/react-slot\": \"1.3.0\",\n    \"@tanstack/react-query\": \"5.101.2\",\n    \"@tanstack/react-router\": \"1.170.16\",\n    \"@tauri-apps/api\": \"2.12.4\",\n    \"@trpc/client\": \"11.18.0\",\n    \"@trpc/react-query\": \"11.18.0\",\n    \"@trpc/server\": \"11.18.0\",\n    \"class-variance-authority\": \"0.7.1\",\n    \"clsx\": \"2.1.1\",\n    \"dompurify\": \"3.4.17\",\n    \"lucide-react\": \"0.525.0\",\n    \"mermaid\": \"11.16.0\",\n    \"qrcode.react\": \"4.2.0\",\n    \"react\": \"19.2.3\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"19.2.3\",\n    \"sanitize-html\": \"2.17.5\",\n    \"superjson\": \"2.2.6\",\n    \"tailwind-merge\": \"3.6.0\",\n    \"zustand\": \"5.0.14\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@tailwindcss/vite\": \"4.3.2\",\n    \"@tauri-apps/cli\": \"2.12.3\",\n    \"@testing-library/dom\": \"10.4.1\",\n    \"@testing-library/jest-dom\": \"6.9.1\",\n    \"@testing-library/react\": \"16.3.2\",\n    \"@testing-library/user-event\": \"14.6.1\",\n    \"@types/react\": \"19.2.17\",\n    \"@types/react-dom\": \"19.2.3\",\n    \"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"5.2.0\",\n    \"jsdom\": \"25.0.1\",\n    \"tailwindcss\": \"4.3.2\",\n    \"typescript\": \"5.9.3\",\n    \"vite\": \"7.3.6\",\n    \"vitest\": \"3.2.6\"\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"name\": \"@prisma-airs/desktop-contracts\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"license\": \"Apache-2.0\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"exports\": {\n    \".\": \"./src/index.ts\",\n    \"./fixtures/wire/*\": \"./fixtures/wire/*\",\n    \"./fixtures/academy/*\": \"./fixtures/academy/*\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"typescript\": \"5.9.3\"\n  }\n}\n[toolchain]\nchannel = \"1.99.0\"\ntargets = [\"aarch64-apple-darwin\"]\ncomponents = [\"rustfmt\", \"clippy\"]\nprofile = \"minimal\"\n/**\n * Academy's learner pages keep presentation-only state in WebView storage\n * under `academy-` keys: the per-account completion-moment latch\n * (`academy-completion-moments:<accountId>`) and the unit contents rail\n * preference. Server truth always wins, so the latch survives sign-out as\n * on Academy web; a completed local-data reset forgets it with everything\n * else the desktop kept about the learner.\n */\nexport const ACADEMY_STORAGE_PREFIX = 'academy-'\n\n/** Removes every Academy presentation key; returns how many were removed. */\nexport function forgetAcademyPresentation(storage: Storage | undefined = globalThis.localStorage): number {\n    if (!storage) return 0\n    try {\n        const keys: string[] = []\n        for (let i = 0; i < storage.length; i += 1) {\n            const key = storage.key(i)\n            if (key?.startsWith(ACADEMY_STORAGE_PREFIX)) keys.push(key)\n        }\n        for (const key of keys) storage.removeItem(key)\n        return keys.length\n    } catch {\n        // Storage unavailable: nothing was kept there.\n        return 0\n    }\n}\n        use std::os::unix::fs::{DirBuilderExt, PermissionsExt};\n        fs::DirBuilder::new()\n            .recursive(true)\n            .mode(0o700)\n            .create(dir)\n            .map_err(|_| StoreError::Unavailable)?;\n        let meta = fs::symlink_metadata(dir).map_err(|_| StoreError::Unavailable)?;\n        if !meta.is_dir() {\n            return Err(StoreError::Unavailable);\n        }\n        fs::set_permissions(dir, fs::Permissions::from_mode(0o700))\n            .map_err(|_| StoreError::Unavailable)?;\n        let lock = open_owner_only(&dir.join(LOCK_FILE), false)?;\n        lock.try_lock().map_err(|_| StoreError::Unavailable)?;\n        Ok(Self {\n            dir: dir.to_owned(),\n            _lock: lock,\n            #[cfg(any(test, feature = \"test-fixtures\"))]\n            fault: std::sync::Mutex::new(None),\n        })\n    }\n\n    fn path(&self) -> PathBuf {\n        self.dir.join(STATE_FILE)\n    }\n\n    #[cfg(any(test, feature = \"test-fixtures\"))]\n    pub fn inject(&self, fault: Option<StoreFault>) {\n        if let Ok(mut f) = self.fault.lock() {\n            *f = fault;\n        }\n    }\n\n    #[cfg(any(test, feature = \"test-fixtures\"))]\n    fn faulted(&self, point: StoreFault) -> bool {\n        self.fault\n            .lock()\n            .map(|f| *f == Some(point))\n            .unwrap_or(false)\n    }\n\n    #[cfg(not(any(test, feature = \"test-fixtures\")))]\n    fn faulted(&self, _: StoreFault) -> bool {\n        false\n    }\n\n    fn sync_dir(&self) -> Result<(), StoreError> {\n        if self.faulted(StoreFault::AfterRename) {\n            return Err(StoreError::Unconfirmed);\n        }\n        File::open(&self.dir)\n            .and_then(|d| d.sync_all())\n            .map_err(|_| StoreError::Unconfirmed)\n    }\n}\n\nfn open_owner_only(path: &Path, truncate: bool) -> Result<File, StoreError> {\n    use std::os::unix::fs::OpenOptionsExt;\n    OpenOptions::new()\n        .read(true)\n        .write(true)\n        .create(true)\n        .truncate(truncate)\n        .mode(0o600)\n        .custom_flags(libc_nofollow())\n        .open(path)\n        .map_err(|_| StoreError::Unavailable)\n}\n\n/// `O_NOFOLLOW` (macOS `<sys/fcntl.h>` value): never open through a planted\n/// symlink. The desktop targets macOS only.\n#[cfg(target_os = \"macos\")]\nfn libc_nofollow() -> i32 {\n    0x0100\n}\n\nimpl AppStore for FileStore {\n    fn load(&self) -> Result<Option<PersistedState>, StoreError> {\n        let path = self.path();\n        let meta = match fs::symlink_metadata(&path) {\n            Ok(meta) => meta,\n            Err(e) if e.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound => return Ok(None),\n            Err(_) => return Err(StoreError::Unavailable),\n        };\n        if !meta.is_file() || meta.len() > MAX_STATE_BYTES {\n            return Err(StoreError::Corrupt);\n        }\n        let mut bytes = Vec::new();\n        File::open(&path)\n            .and_then(|f| f.take(MAX_STATE_BYTES + 1).read_to_end(&mut bytes))\n            .map_err(|_| StoreError::Unavailable)?;\n        let state: PersistedState =\n            serde_json::from_slice(&bytes).map_err(|_| StoreError::Corrupt)?;\n        if !state.is_consistent() {\n            return Err(StoreError::Corrupt);\n        }\n        Ok(Some(state))\n    }\n\n    fn save(&self, state: &PersistedState) -> Result<(), StoreError> {\n        let bytes = serde_json::to_vec_pretty(state).map_err(|_| StoreError::Unavailable)?;\n        let mut entropy = [0u8; 8];\n        getrandom::fill(&mut entropy).map_err(|_| StoreError::Unavailable)?;\n        let temp = self\n            .dir\n            .join(format!(\".{STATE_FILE}.{}\", hex::encode(entropy)));\n        // Before the rename nothing has changed (Unavailable); after it the\n        // new document is in place and only its durability is unconfirmed.\n        let replaced = (|| {\n            let mut file = open_owner_only(&temp, true)?;\n            file.write_all(&bytes)\n                .map_err(|_| StoreError::Unavailable)?;\n            file.sync_all().map_err(|_| StoreError::Unavailable)?;\n            if self.faulted(StoreFault::BeforeRename) {\n                return Err(StoreError::Unavailable);\n            }\n            fs::rename(&temp, self.path()).map_err(|_| StoreError::Unavailable)\n        })();\n        if replaced.is_err() {\n            let _ = fs::remove_file(&temp);\n            return replaced;\n        }\n        self.sync_dir()\n    }\n\n    fn reset(&self) -> Result<(), StoreError> {\n        match fs::remove_file(self.path()) {\n            Ok(()) => {}\n            Err(e) if e.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound => {}\n            Err(_) => return Err(StoreError::Unavailable),\n        }\n        self.sync_dir()\n    }\n}\n\n/// The store used when the data directory cannot be opened (for example\n/// another instance holds its lease): every call reports `Unavailable`, so\n/// the snapshot says so and nothing is written elsewhere.\npub struct UnavailableStore;\n\nimpl AppStore for UnavailableStore {\n    fn load(&self) -> Result<Option<PersistedState>, StoreError> {\n        Err(StoreError::Unavailable)\n    }\n\n    fn save(&self, _: &PersistedState) -> Result<(), StoreError> {\n        Err(StoreError::Unavailable)\n    }\n\n    fn reset(&self) -> Result<(), StoreError> {\n        Err(StoreError::Unavailable)\n    }\n}\n\n/// In-memory store for builds and tests that must not touch the disk.\n#[derive(Default)]\npub struct MemoryStore {\n    state: std::sync::Mutex<Option<PersistedState>>,\n}\n\nimpl MemoryStore {\n    pub fn new() -> Self {\n        Self::default()\n    }\n}\n\nimpl AppStore for MemoryStore {\n    fn load(&self) -> Result<Option<PersistedState>, StoreError> {\n        self.state\n            .lock()\n            .map(|s| s.clone())\n            .map_err(|_| StoreError::Unavailable)\n    }\n\n    fn save(&self, state: &PersistedState) -> Result<(), StoreError> {\n        *self.state.lock().map_err(|_| StoreError::Unavailable)? = Some(state.clone());\n        Ok(())\n    }\n\n    fn reset(&self) -> Result<(), StoreError> {\n        *self.state.lock().map_err(|_| StoreError::Unavailable)? = None;\n        Ok(())\n    }\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n    use crate::tenants::{Destination, Region};\n\n    fn scratch(name: &str) -> PathBuf {\n        let mut entropy = [0u8; 6];\n        getrandom::fill(&mut entropy).expect(\"entropy\");\n        std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(\"airs-v2-store-{name}-{}\", hex::encode(entropy)))\n    }\n\n    fn sample() -> PersistedState {\n        let id = TenantId::parse(\"tn-0123456789abcdef\").expect(\"id\");\n        PersistedState {\n            appearance: Theme::Dark,\n            tenants: vec![TenantProfile {\n//! Rust-owned application storage for nonsecret desktop state.\n//!\n//! One versioned JSON document holds the appearance preference, tenant\n//! profiles, the active tenant, the Keychain credential index (record IDs and\n//! their bound destinations, never secrets) and the pending cleanup ledger.\n//! Session-only credentials are never written. The file store uses an\n//! owner-only directory and file, atomic replacement (temporary file, fsync,\n//! rename, directory fsync) and an exclusive lock file held for the store's\n//! lifetime, so a second instance cannot interleave writes. An unreadable\n//! document is reported as corrupt and left untouched until the operator\n//! explicitly resets local data.\n\nuse std::collections::BTreeSet;\nuse std::fs::{self, File, OpenOptions};\nuse std::io::{Read, Write};\nuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n\nuse crate::tenants::{TenantId, TenantProfile};\nuse crate::vault::RecordId;\nuse crate::wire::Theme;\n\n/// Schema of the persisted state document.\npub const STATE_SCHEMA: &str = \"prisma-airs-desktop/state/1\";\n/// Ceiling for the persisted document.\npub const MAX_STATE_BYTES: u64 = 4 * 1024 * 1024;\nconst STATE_FILE: &str = \"state.json\";\nconst LOCK_FILE: &str = \"state.lock\";\n\n/// Which capability a credential authorizes (D013: a management\n/// registration never supplies scan authentication, nor the reverse).\n#[derive(\n    Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord, Hash, Serialize, Deserialize,\n)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\npub enum CredentialClass {\n    /// The tenant's AIRS runtime scan key.\n    #[default]\n    Scan,\n    /// The tenant's management OAuth client secret (C08).\n    Management,\n    /// A Gateway workspace inference key (C18): used only for that\n    /// workspace's inference, sent only to its runtime endpoint.\n    Inference,\n}\n\n/// A Keychain credential the core may use after restart.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\", deny_unknown_fields)]\npub struct StoredCredential {\n    pub record: RecordId,\n    pub tenant: TenantId,\n    /// The approved origin this credential may be sent to (the scan origin,\n    /// or the management OAuth token origin).\n    pub destination: String,\n    /// The capability it authorizes (scan when absent, as before C08).\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub class: CredentialClass,\n    /// The management OAuth client ID (management credentials only).\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n    pub client_id: Option<String>,\n    /// The workspace and runtime endpoint an inference key is for\n    /// (inference credentials only; the destination is that endpoint).\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n    pub inference: Option<crate::gateway_inference::InferenceTarget>,\n}\n\n/// The signed-in Academy learner account (nonsecret; the refresh token is in\n/// the learner Keychain namespace under `record`).\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\", deny_unknown_fields)]\npub struct StoredLearner {\n    pub account_id: String,\n    pub display_name: String,\n    pub record: RecordId,\n    /// The issuer and public client the session was granted by.\n    pub issuer: String,\n    pub client_id: String,\n}\n\n/// The Gateway workspace a tenant last chose (C16; nonsecret).\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\", deny_unknown_fields)]\npub struct GatewayPreference {\n    pub tenant: TenantId,\n    pub workspace: String,\n}\n\n/// A tenant's company sign-in for the Harness Gateway credential (C20;\n/// nonsecret: the refresh token is in the Keychain under `grant.record`).\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\", deny_unknown_fields)]\npub struct StoredSignIn {\n    pub tenant: TenantId,\n    /// The Gateway workspace and runtime endpoint the token is used for.\n    pub target: crate::gateway_inference::InferenceTarget,\n    pub issuer: String,\n    pub client_id: String,\n    pub audience: String,\n    /// The Harness uses this sign-in rather than the workspace key.\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub selected: bool,\n    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n    pub grant: Option<StoredGrant>,\n}\n\n/// A signed-in account: the stable grant a conversation is bound to.\n/// Renewals keep it; signing out ends it and a new sign-in is a new grant.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\", deny_unknown_fields)]\npub struct StoredGrant {\n    pub id: String,\n    pub subject: String,\n    pub label: String,\n    pub record: RecordId,\n}\n\n/// A tenant's Harness project folder (C21; nonsecret).\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\", deny_unknown_fields)]\npub struct StoredProject {\n    pub tenant: TenantId,\n    /// Canonical absolute path.\n    pub path: String,\n    /// Changes in it are allowed, each with the operator's approval.\n    pub write: bool,\n}\n\n/// A workspace MCP server a tenant uses with the Harness (C22; nonsecret).\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\", deny_unknown_fields)]\npub struct StoredMcpServer {\n    pub tenant: TenantId,\n    /// The Gateway workspace it is published in.\n    pub workspace: String,\n    pub server_id: String,\n    /// On for new conversations (at most eight per workspace).\n    pub enabled: bool,\n    pub grant: Option<StoredMcpGrant>,\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as directory:\n            root=Path(directory);path=root/\"docs/planning/evidence/P10\";path.mkdir(parents=True)\n            proof=dict(schema=\"airs-desktop/p10-completion-proof/1\",p09={\"subject\":\"P09\"},p10={\"subject\":\"P10\"},attempt=\"attempt-01\",source_archive=\"docs/planning/evidence/P10/source-archive\")\n            (path/\"completion-proof.json\").write_text(json.dumps(proof))\n            with patch.object(review_gate,\"actual_review\",side_effect=[proof[\"p09\"],proof[\"p10\"]]):\n                with self.assertRaises(KeyError):review_gate.release_prerequisites(root)\n\n    def test_actual_historical_transport_and_reject_output_mutations(self):\n        import json,shutil\n        root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n        original=root/\"docs/planning/reviews/P09/attempt-02\"\n        request=json.loads((original/\"request.json\").read_text())\n        request[\"execution_root\"]=json.loads((root/\"docs/planning/evidence/C45/activation-20261102-g11/p09-proof.json\").read_text())[\"source_checkout\"]\n        request[\"schema_archive\"]=\"docs/planning/evidence/C45/activation-20261102-g11/p09-source/docs/architecture/review-verdict.schema.json\"\n        self.assertTrue(review_gate.transport(root,original,request)[\"reviewer_sessions_observed\"])\n        for flag,wrong in [(\"-o\",\"/wrong/verdict.json\"),(\"--output-schema\",\"/wrong/schema.json\"),(\"-s\",\"workspace-write\")]:\n            with self.subTest(flag=flag),tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as directory:\n                out=Path(directory)\n                for name in [\"invocation.json\",\"request.json\",\"feature-probe.log\",\"thread-reply.log\",\"verdict-returned.json\"]:shutil.copy2(original/name,out/name)\n                invocation=json.loads((out/\"invocation.json\").read_text());args=invocation[\"command_without_prompt\"];args[args.index(flag)+1]=wrong\n                (out/\"invocation.json\").write_text(json.dumps(invocation))\n                with self.assertRaisesRegex(ValueError,\"transport\"):review_gate.transport(root,out,request)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":unittest.main()\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
